<title>BELGIUM: DELHAIZE 1996 GROUP NET PROFIT UP 15%.</title>
<headline>DELHAIZE 1996 GROUP NET PROFIT UP 15%.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)    4.354   vs   3.767</p>
<p>    Cons net				   8.172   vs   6.806</p>
<p>    Consolidated sales		   412.346   vs 368.478</p>
<p>    Cons cashflow from operations     24.287   vs  20.256</p>
<p>    Operating income			16.687   vs  13.688</p>
<p>    Exceptional loss			 0.031   vs   0.082</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs/share)	    27    vs     25</p>
<p>NOTE: Etablissements Delhaize Freres et Cie &quot;Le Lion&quot; SA</p>
<p>is a leading Belgian retail group.</p>
<p>    Shareholders equity		   28.200   vs  23.980</p>
<p>ratios:</p>
<p>    cashflow/cons sales		  5.89 pct  vs   5.50 pct</p>
<p>    cons profit/cons sales	     1.98 pct  vs   1.85 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: Delhaize said the 11.9 percent rise in consolidated</p>
<p>sales would have been eight percent at comparable exchange</p>
<p>rates. The rise of 15.6 percent in group net profit would have</p>
<p>been 11.7 at comparable rates.</p>
<p>At the end of 1996 the Delhaize group operated 1,700 sales</p>
<p>outlets in five countries, after 124 stores were opened during</p>
<p>the financial year.</p>
<p>Performance by division:</p>
<p>Delhaize &quot;Le Lion&quot; (billions of Belgian francs):</p>
<p>    Sales (inc VAT)		   106.970	  +3.4 pct</p>
<p>    Net profit			    1.929	 +21.1 pct</p>
<p>Despite stagnant consumption and increased competition,</p>
<p>Delhaize increased market share of total food sales in Belgium</p>
<p>to 13.2 percent from 13.0 percent at the end of 1995. Net profit</p>
<p>was boosted by strong growth in income from investments.</p>
<p>Food Lion (millions of dollars):</p>
<p>    Sales			     9,005.9	    +9.7 pct</p>
<p>    Net profit			  206.1	   +19.6 pct</p>
<p>Figures from Kash n' Karry, acquired in December 1995 will</p>
<p>be consolidated in Delhaize accounts from 1997. Delhaize said</p>
<p>expansion for Food Lion remained focused on internal expansion,</p>
<p>modernisation and enlargement of existing stores, and</p>
<p>acquisition.</p>
<p>Super Discount Markets U.S.A. (millions of dollars):</p>
<p>    Sales				 274.8	    -6.1 pct</p>
<p>    Net profit			    0.25	  -37.6 pct</p>
<p>P.G. Group (millions of French francs):</p>
<p>    Sales				2,082.4	   +6.3 pct</p>
<p>    Net profit			    33.7	   -3.1</p>
<p>Profit was weighed down by the payment of a non-recurring</p>
<p>indemnity of 6.2 million francs for the early repayment of</p>
<p>long-term loans.</p>
<p>Alfa-Beta (billions of drachma):</p>
<p>    Sales				   95.3	   +16.8 pct</p>
<p>    Net profit			     1		+6.9 pct</p>
<p>Delvita (millions of Czech crowns):</p>
<p>    Sales				3,704	     +55 pct</p>
<p>    Net loss				12.5	    -8.3 pct</p>
<p>Net results were depressed by unspecified, expansion-</p>
<p>related charges.</p>
<p>-- Lorrayne Smith, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6812, Fax +32</p>
<p>2 230 7710</p>
</text>
